<DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" Id="example1">
    <div>
        Each item is an icon over its text, and a link when it has a <b>Url</b>. A custom item type is read through
        <b>NameSelectors</b>, which maps each field of the navbar onto a property of that type. In the default
        <b>Automatic</b> mode the item whose URL matches the current page is selected and marked
        <code>aria-current="page"</code>.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarCustoms"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>IsEnabled</b> disables the whole navbar, and the <b>IsEnabled</b> selector a single item. A disabled item
        loses its link and its tab stop, and is announced as dimmed.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>Disabled navbar:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarCustoms" IsEnabled="false"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Disabled item:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarCustomsDisabled"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName },
                                            IsEnabled = { Selector = item => item.Disabled is false } })" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Manual Mode" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        In the <b>Manual</b> mode clicks select the items instead of the URL, for a navbar that switches panels of one
        page. <b>DefaultSelectedItem</b> sets the starting item.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="container">
        <BitNavBar Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="basicNavBarCustoms"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarCustoms[0]"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="URL Matching" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example4CsharpCode" Id="example4" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>Match</b> (per navbar, or per item through its selector) compares URLs <b>Exact</b>ly (the default), by
        <b>Prefix</b>, as a <b>Wildcard</b> pattern (<b>?</b>, <b>*</b> within a segment, <b>**</b> across segments) or
        as a <b>Regex</b>. Exact and Prefix ignore case and a trailing slash. The <b>AdditionalUrls</b> selector gives an
        item more URLs to match. All of these are matched against the URL of this page.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>Exact (the default):</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="exactMatchCustoms"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName },
                                            Url = { Selector = item => item.Link } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Prefix:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="prefixMatchCustoms" Match="BitNavMatch.Prefix"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName },
                                            Url = { Selector = item => item.Link } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Wildcard:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="wildcardMatchCustoms"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName },
                                            Url = { Selector = item => item.Link },
                                            Match = { Selector = item => item.Matching },
                                            IsEnabled = { Selector = item => item.Disabled is false } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Regex:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="regexMatchCustoms"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName },
                                            Url = { Selector = item => item.Link },
                                            Match = { Selector = item => item.Matching },
                                            IsEnabled = { Selector = item => item.Disabled is false } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>AdditionalUrls:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="additionalUrlsCustoms"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName },
                                            Url = { Selector = item => item.Link },
                                            AdditionalUrls = { Selector = item => item.ExtraLinks } })" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Labels" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>IconOnly</b> hides every label, <b>HideUnselectedText</b> keeps only the selected one's, and
        <b>InlineText</b> puts the label beside the icon. A hidden label still names its item for screen readers.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>IconOnly:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarCustoms" IconOnly
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>HideUnselectedText:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar HideUnselectedText
                   Mode="BitNavMode.Manual"
                   Items="basicNavBarCustoms"
                   DefaultSelectedItem="basicNavBarCustoms[0]"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>InlineText:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarCustoms" InlineText
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Width & Alignment" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        <b>FitWidth</b> shrinks the navbar to its content and <b>FullWidth</b> stretches it over its container.
        <b>Justified</b> gives every item an equal share, and <b>Alignment</b> packs or spreads the items along the bar.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>FitWidth:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarCustoms" FitWidth
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>FullWidth:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="basicNavBarCustoms" FullWidth
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Justified (labels of unequal length):</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Items="unevenNavBarCustoms" Justified
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Alignment Center:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Alignment="BitAlignment.Center" Items="basicNavBarCustoms"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div>Alignment SpaceBetween:</div><br />
    <div class="container short">
        <BitNavBar Alignment="BitAlignment.SpaceBetween" Items="basicNavBarCustoms"
                   NameSelectors="@(new() { Text = { Selector = item => item.Title },
                                            IconName = { Selector = item => item.ImageName } })" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Selection" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example7CsharpCode" Id="example7" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        The <b>SelectedIconName</b> selector (or <b>SelectedIcon</b>) swaps the selected item to a filled glyph.
        <b>Filled</b> fills the hovered and selected item with the <b>Color</b>, and <b>Indicator</b> adds a <b>Line</b>
        along its edge or a <b>Pill</b> behind its icon - cues beyond color alone.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div>SelectedIconName:</div><br />
